{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>At that time. And the sackcloth.</b> As a sign that the prophet was wearing sackcloth. And this is a difficult question: how could the prophet go naked to be a sign concerning Egypt? And I shall explain it at the beginning of Trei Asar [Hosea], with the help of HaShem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:25.907651409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}